A||||2||RobertVol||HEre is a new one to me...????||||1||
Z||000000||RobertVol||03-13-2001||11:24 AM||||My 88gt was having some problems a few months back. I pulled the code and it was the EGR Valve. Checked it out and it was completely faulty. I replaced the entire system and it ran good for awhile. Then about a month ago I was driving it down the interstate at the 60-70 mph range and the Check engine light comes on. hmmmm <P>Thinking it maybe the EGR again. Other than that no other performance issues. There was a strong smell of gas though.<P>Now a few days ago the car starting bucking and then completely died on me. I could not get it to start at at all. It seemed there was getting no spark. SOOOOOO hmmmmm<P>I took it to a friends shop and he tells me EGR Code again. I said that doesn not explain the dieing completely and not starting at all. So with a little tracking down I found that the ignition coil was shot!<P>TADA!! now my question for all of this is:<P>Would the ignition coil going out cause the EGR code to be thrown? Because now I have the codes cleared out and the new coil and now I have ran it hard and down the interstate and no codes are thrown with the new coil on. Other than I still haven't found a shop that can set the idle PROPERLY on our cars!! The car runs fine! <P>Let me know what ya think<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||03-13-2001||12:17 PM||||If the coil was getting weaker, It may have caused unburnt gas to be expelled. This would mess up the oxygen sensors readings and it is possible the ECM assumed it was the EGR causing the problem. It would assume the unburnt gas was due to EGR not opening when required.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RobertVol||03-13-2001||12:56 PM||||Ahhh Orief.... Good point... Now I got to do is find a good ignition coil. I know some think its not worth it but I think a MSD or Jacobs would help a little .... ||||reg||1
